out_dxf: terminate the cquote() result after the last written character

cquote() only wrote a NUL into the last byte of the malloc'ed destination
buffer, so strlen() in dxf_fixup_string() read uninitialized memory between
the end of the quoted text and the end of the buffer. With a fresh, zeroed
heap (e.g. native Windows) this is invisible; with a reused heap (WebAssembly
dlmalloc) random bytes were appended to strings containing a newline, e.g.
TOLERANCE text "...%%v^J10" became "...%%v^J10\U+B10Djsj...".

--- a/src/out_dxf.c
+++ b/src/out_dxf.c
@@ -1370,7 +1370,9 @@
       else
         *dest++ = c;
     }
+  if (dest < dend)
+    *dest = '\0'; // terminate after the last written char
   d[len - 1] = '\0'; // add final delim, skipped above
   return d;
 }
